A ready thread bound to a share is not put on the share's ring.
It would never get the processor;
every ready thread with a share but the running one is on its share's ring.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a waiting or ready thread is on no queue

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -178,9 +178,6 @@ void sched_bind(struct thread *t, uint32_t share, struct cap *parent)
     }
     t->share = (struct cap){ .type = CAP_BOUND, .rights = RIGHT_W, .a = share };
     cap_attach(parent, &t->share);
-    if (t->state == THREAD_READY && t != current) {
-        enqueue(t);
-    }
 }
 
 void sched_unbind(struct cap *bound)
